{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.GroebnerShirshovEnergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.GroebnerShirshovEnergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeStep_can_lower_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeStep_can_lower_energy","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L202-L210","doc":"**The `.md` claim \"every Hecke step increases the energy\" is false.**\nOn `σ₁σ₁` with `h = 1/5` the energy drops. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeStep_energy_change","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeStep_energy_change","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L180-L200","doc":"**Energy change of one Hecke step** on an isolated monomial\n`c · u σᵢσᵢ v ↦ c h · u σᵢ v + c · u v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.wordEnergy_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.wordEnergy_single","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L176-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.energyPath_telescopes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.energyPath_telescopes","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L162-L174","doc":"**Path independence (telescoping).** For any path of states, the sum of\nthe step changes is the energy of the last state minus that of the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.wordEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.wordEnergy","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L158-L160","doc":"Energy of a linear combination of braid words: `Σ_w |c_w| · ℓ(w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.groebner_shirshov_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.groebner_shirshov_energy","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L137-L140","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:groebner-shirshov-energy","label":"thm:groebner-shirshov-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_energy_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_energy_negative","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L122-L135","doc":"The beta-decay energy difference is always negative:\nthe daughter has lower energy than the parent.\n(Computationally verified for all A ≤ 6.)\n\n**Was an axiom; now proved (2026-11-15).** As stated, the two reals\nare existentially quantified and not tied to any parent or daughter,\nso `1` and `0` witness it. The intended content (the energies of the\nactual parent and daughter normal forms) is open in Lean, bean\n`qou-n2un`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.not_energy_path_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.not_energy_path_independent","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**The former axiom is false.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.totalEnergyChange_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.totalEnergyChange_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L88-L98","doc":"The total energy is non-negative for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.totalEnergyChange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.totalEnergyChange","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The total energy change is the sum of Hecke step energies.\nYang-Baxter and far commutativity contribute zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stepEnergyChange_hecke_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stepEnergyChange_hecke_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The step hypothesis in the two results above is load-bearing: the remaining\nconstructor genuinely moves energy, so neither statement holds for an\narbitrary `step`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.farComm_energy_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.farComm_energy_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L58-L62","doc":"Far commutativity steps have zero energy change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.yangBaxter_energy_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.yangBaxter_energy_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L52-L56","doc":"Yang-Baxter steps have zero energy change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stepEnergyChange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stepEnergyChange","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L42-L50","doc":"The energy change of a single division step carrying coefficient `coeff`.\nOnly the Hecke relation moves energy; Yang-Baxter and far commutativity are\nenergy-preserving. This is the per-step form of the `.hecke`-only filter\nused by `energy_path_independent` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeEnergyChange_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeEnergyChange_pos","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L32-L40","doc":"The energy change is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeEnergyChange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeEnergyChange","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L27-L30","doc":"The energy change per Hecke step: |c| × (q - q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.farComm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.farComm","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.yangBaxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.yangBaxter","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType.hecke","kind":"ctor","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L23-L23","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DivisionStepType","kind":"inductive","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/groebner-shirshov-energy.lean#L20-L25","doc":"A single division step in the Gröbner reduction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}